      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "PURPOSE",
          "content": "To examine if preoperative diclofenac 50 mg or diazepam 10 mg po are useful adjuncts to spinal anesthesia for day-case varicose vein repair."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Two hundred ASA physical status I-II outpatients, age 18-60 yr, were randomized to receive either diclofenac 50 mg po or diazepam 10 mg po one hour before operation in a double-blind fashion (100 patients in both groups). If the patient was distressed or feared the spinal puncture and requested sedation, a bolus dose of alfentanil 0.5 mg was given i.v. as a rescue medication. On request, patients received diclofenac 50 mg po and, when needed, oxycodone 0.1 mg x kg(-1) im for postoperative pain relief. They were discharged with a supply of diclofenac 50 mg tablets and were asked to record postoperative pain using a visual analogue scale (VAS) and quantity of tablets taken."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The VAS scores (+/- SD) eight hours after surgery, the next morning, and in the morning and at the end of the first and second postoperative days were 23 +/- 21, 12 +/- 17, 11 +/- 15, 8 +/- 15 and 8 +/- 15 in the diclofenac group, and 24 +/- 23, 12 +/- 20, 10 +/- 17, 8 +/- 16 and 7 +/- 14 in the diazepam group, respectively (NS). In the diclofenac and diazepam groups, 31% and 67% of the patients required postoperative diclofenac during the first eight postoperative hours (P <0.05). Diazepam premedication did not alter the number of patients who required alfentanil before spinal puncture."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Diclofenac premedication reduced the analgesic requirements during the first eight hours after varicose vein repair."
        }
      ]},
